We can compute $837 \times 750$ by breaking it down into factors using its place value.

Let $837$ be represented as $800 + 30 + 7$. Hence we can break $837$ as
\begin{align*}
837 &= 800 + 30 + 7.
\end{align*}
Thus
\begin{align*}
837 \times 750 &= (800 + 30 + 7) \times 750 \\
&= 800 \times 750 + 30 \times 750 + 7 \times 750 \\
&= 600,000 + 22,500 + 5,250 \\
&= 637,750.
\end{align*}
This solves the problem. The answer is 637,750

